        "title": "An eye and mind-opening experience",
        "text": "To the western eye and mind the Pashupatinath Temple may be a bit jarring. The idea of watching the mourning as well the mourned as bodies are cremated is quite foreign to the typical western ideas around death, however, there is something quite humbling and beautiful about witnessing this. A guide is definitely helpful here, but be cautious of the men who will offer you information and chat expecting to be paid. If you're going to pay someone just choose carefully, but hearing the history from others is definitely helpful. Also be prepared that \"holy men\" will expect compensation for allowing you to take their photos. ",
