        "title": "Worth a visit",
        "text": "Pashupath is very different from anything you will see in the west - part temple complex, part public cremation site. The temples are worth seeing but unless you are hindu you are not allowed into the main temple.\n\nThe best view of the whole complex is from the steps on the other side of the river, opposite the Royal Ghats. You can closer views of the cremations if you wish from the bridge. Families do not seem to mind, but it is best not to be too intrusive. It is probably better to visit in December or January when the river is higher as there is a fair amount of rubbish in it which is revealed when it is low.",
