        "title": "LOOK WITH APPRECIATION, NOT VOYEURISM",
        "text": "Get rid of any ethnocentricism before you visit Pashupatinath. This is a place where you can learn to appreciate that other people have some quite beautiful, very different ideas to yours. You will see the newly-deceased being cremated; you'll witness the grief of their loved ones, and the care with which they tend the body. Yes, the river is disgusting and dirty, but to the local people it's holy - don't be judgmental. Oh, and watch out for those pretend-sadhus who hang around ready to pose for a photo-for-a-price - real sadhus don't do that!",
