      {
        "review_id": 129122015,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r129122015-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Eerie, but strangely beautiful!",
        "text": "Visiting an open air crematorium is not something you would expect to enjoy, but the Pashupati Nath Temple is one of the holiest temples in the world. Worshipped by Hindus and Buddhists it is an example of religious harmony. The whole area is surrounded by ancient temples of archaeologically and architecturally importance. You cannot help watch (from a distance) the burning of the bodies along the river side, and see the families accept the fate of their loved ones without tears, without sadness but with relief and calm. There was a strange eerie ness of the whole place but it was also beautiful.",
